{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence type of every report and delivery stream the library hands out, and of an app’s own, read by one task at a time."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Reading-reports","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue"],"title":"Reading reports"},{"anchor":"Making-a-queue-of-your-own","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation"],"title":"Making a queue of your own"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/asyncqueues"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"AsyncQueues","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"AsyncQueues"}],"externalID":"AsyncQueues","roleHeading":"Framework"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is what a store’s, a consent’s, a tracker’s, a delivery’s and a destination’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report streams are: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Consent.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.rejectionReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.samplingDropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Delivery.bufferDropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"InMemoryDestination.deliveries","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". You read one with ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as you would any asynchronous","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence. The type that owns the queue fills it and ends it. Your code only reads these.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What arrives while nothing reads waits for the next read, as the owner’s documentation says:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store’s and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":"’s drop reports wait without a bound."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A delivery’s buffer-drop reports merge into one per destination."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracker’s rejection reports merge into one per event, property and keyword."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its sampling drop reports merge into one per event type."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A consent’s drop reports merge only when a held-record-limit report follows another."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"InMemoryDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps only its newest batches."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The queue ends once its owner is gone or finished and every waiting element has been read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One task reads at a time. The first iterator to read holds the queue until its iteration ends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the iterator is released, as it is when its task ends. A holder that stops calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its iterator keeps the turn. A second reader that starts meanwhile logs a warning once and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waits until the first one’s iteration ends or its iterator is released, then reads on from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next element. So the reader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holding the queue gets every element, in order, and nothing traps or takes elements from it. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reader cancelled while it waits returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and leaves the holder alone. To hand every report to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"several parts of the app, read the queue in one task and fan each report out from there."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let reports = store.dropReports","Task {","    for await report in reports {","        logger.warning(\"Dropped: \\(report)\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read the queue into a constant before starting the task, as above, so the task holds the queue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and not its owner."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"A queue of your own","anchor":"A-queue-of-your-own"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Where your app hands out a stream of its own, such as every report merged into one for its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"logging, make it an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncQueue"},{"text":" too, so a second reader of it waits its turn as with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation"},{"text":" is its writing end, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream.Continuation"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stream’s: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/init(name:)"},{"text":" makes a queue that keeps what no one has read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yet without a bound, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/enqueue(_:)"},{"text":" adds an element from any thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without waiting, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/finish()"},{"text":" ends the queue after what it keeps, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does the last copy of the continuation going away. Hand the readers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/queue"},{"text":" and keep the continuation to yourself:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let drops = AsyncQueue<String>.Continuation(name: \"the app's drop reports\")","let storeReports = store.dropReports","Task {","    for await report in storeReports {","        drops.enqueue(\"Not stored: \\(report)\")","    }","    drops.finish()","}","let reads = drops.queue"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The umbrella guide on reading reports is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/gettingstarted"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue":{"url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Elements in the order they are enqueued, kept until they are read; one reader at a time reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"title":"AsyncQueue","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/gettingstarted":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/gettingstarted","type":"link","title":"Getting Started","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Getting Started"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/gettingstarted"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue/Continuation/enqueue(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/enqueue(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enqueue","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hands "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"element"},{"type":"text","text":" to the read waiting for one, or keeps it for the next read; dropped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once the queue is finished."}],"url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue\/continuation\/enqueue(_:)","title":"enqueue(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"AsyncQueues","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The sequence type of every report and delivery stream the library hands out, and of an app’s own, read by one task at a time.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue/Continuation":{"title":"AsyncQueue.Continuation","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Continuation"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Continuation"}],"url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue\/continuation","abstract":[{"text":"The writing end of a queue an app makes: it adds elements and ends the queue, while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/queue"},{"text":" is handed to the code that reads.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue/Continuation/finish()":{"title":"finish()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"finish"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/finish()","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue\/continuation\/finish()","abstract":[{"text":"Ends the queue after the elements it keeps: reads return those, then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":". Elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enqueued after it are dropped.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue/Continuation/init(name:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/init(name:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue\/continuation\/init(name:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"name","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"init(name:)","abstract":[{"text":"A continuation writing to a new, empty queue.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue/Continuation/queue":{"title":"queue","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"queue"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncQueue"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue\/Continuation\/queue","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue\/continuation\/queue","abstract":[{"text":"The queue this continuation writes to, for the code that reads it.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"}}}